def find_Max(arr, low, high):
    # Base case: if the subarray is empty or has only one element, return that element
    if low >= high:
        return arr[low]

    # Find the middle index of the subarray
    mid = (low + high) // 2

    # Check if the middle element is greater than the last element
    if arr[mid] > arr[high]:
        # If the middle element is greater than the last element, the maximum element is in the right half
        return find_Max(arr, mid + 1, high)
    else:
        # If the middle element is less than or equal to the last element, the maximum element is in the left half
        return find_Max(arr, low, mid - 1)
```

